						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Saturday, June 14, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">The SYNDICATE RO Empire is Restored! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hail all,<BR><BR>The most awaited guild event of the century is upon you. The Syndicate Ro Guild has been restored and we are back up and running, with a whole new website and are now recruiting once again. <BR><BR>LEVELS 20 - 65 are invited to join. We are looking for serious roleplayers.<BR><BR>Syndicate Ro is the most organized, complex, and most fun guild created to date. If you don't believe me go to http://www.syndicatero.com and find out for yourself.<BR><BR>Through our website you fill find extensive materials and resources, each member has their own personal web page they can easily update online, with their biography, level, stats, skills, and so much more!<BR><BR>Our ranking structure is the most complex and original idea in guild history.<BR><BR>We are building more than a guild, we're building a community... a society... an empire. And we are far more than loot and levels, so you must be serious about roleplaying.<BR><BR>If you visit the website syndicatero.com  you'll see what I'm talking about.<BR><BR>Long Live Syndicate Ro.<BR><BR>Prince Venefix Dominixomnis
							<br><BR>
							 - syndicatero<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=393">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, June 12, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Girls Guild </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hi you Solusekers.  There is a new guild on the server, and it's a girls only guild!  We have submitted our application and expect approval today or tomorrow.<BR><BR>There are no other requirements other then playing a girl character and being a girl in real life (or be so good at faking it that we couldn't tell, lol).<BR><BR>If you're interested in joining, please see Morainne, Sadava, Proc or Doamna in the game.<BR><BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - LdyNora<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=392">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=392">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, June 10, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Blood Tide Recruiting </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Blood Tide is currently recruiting. We are looking for dedicated and raid oriented individuals that are looking for a close knit, family environment, tempered with discipline and integrity. Loot and personal gain should not be a top priority for you as we award items based on merit and service to the guild and it's members. Those that put in the most will get the most out of membership in Blood Tide.<BR><BR>If you are seeking a quick completion to your epic, look elsewhere. We are focused on building a team that will weather the storms of Everquest and pull together and grow with the game towards the high end.<BR><BR>Minimum Requirements: (no exceptions, so don't ask)<BR><BR>BARDS: 55+<BR>BEASTLORDS: 55+<BR>CLERICS: 56+<BR>DRUIDS: 55+<BR>ENCHANTERS: 55+<BR>MAGICIANS: 55+<BR>MONKS: 55+<BR>NECROMANCERS: 58+<BR>PALADINS: 55+<BR>RANGERS: 55+<BR>ROGUES: 55+<BR>SHAMANS: 58+<BR>SHADOWKNIGHTS: 55+<BR>WARRIORS: 55+<BR>WIZARDS: 55+<BR><BR>Unbuffed Magic Resist: 100+<BR>Unbuffed  Fire Resist: 100+<BR>Unbuffed  Cold Resist: 100+<BR><BR>Required Keys: Sebilis<BR><BR>Required PoP Flags: None<BR><BR>Required Faction: Positive Claws Of Veeshan<BR><BR>http://www.bloodtide.com
							<br><BR>
							 - Zalbar The Mad<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=390">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, June 06, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Hey Sol Ro!  </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							EQ has some great new changes happening... and so do we!<BR><BR>Ganza is making some exciting, new changes little by little to the Site.<BR><BR>I for one am looking forward to seeing the changes as they come!
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=387">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, June 02, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Die Soeldner - New Website </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hi all, just wanted to let you know that Die Soeldner has a new website for the Everquest Folks.<BR><BR>You can visit us at http://eq.diesoeldner.de<BR><BR>PS: Could the Admin of the guildlist please change the link in the guildlist? Thx!
							<br><BR>
							 - Rurulet<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=386">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=386">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, May 29, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">EQ Pixel Army Unveiled </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							<center><BR><div align="left"><table border="3" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="433" height="374" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" bordercolor="#008000" bordercolorlight="#008000" bordercolordark="#008000"><tr><td width="503" height="372"><p align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS" color="#008000"><img border="0" src="http://24.26.194.252:13752/images/banners/eqpixelbanner.jpg" width="450" height="65"></font></p><BR><p align="center"><font size="3" face="Comic Sans MS" color="#008000"><b>After several months of much dedication, the EQ Pixel Army crew has unveiled their project!</b></font></p><BR><p align="center"><font size="3" face="Comic Sans MS" color="#008000"><b>Go look, play, create and experience</b></font></p><BR><p align="center"><font color="#008000"><b><a href="http://www.eqpixelarmy.com/"><font size="4" face="Comic Sans MS">The Gnomish Portrait Machine</font></a><font size="4" face="Comic Sans MS">!</font></b></font></p><BR><p align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS" color="#008000"><b>http://www.eqpixelarmy.com/</b></font></p><BR><p align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS" color="#008000"><img border="0" src="http://24.26.194.252:13752/images/banners/adrasiggif.gif" width="173" height="178"></font></p></td></tr></table></div></center>
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=385">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, May 21, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">EQ Lounge </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							There are (approx) 177 days left until EverQuest II is released.<BR><BR>According to a SOE executive, the beta will definitely begin this summer. If you would like to be notified when the EQII beta begins, simply visit the site and enter your email into the "Newsletter" box. <BR><BR>We would like to inform you that we just opened our EverQuest II discussion forums. The first thread discusses the likely hood and pros/cons of naming the EQII servers after the current EverQuest servers. Stop by and give us your thoughts. Feel free to start any new discussions you feel would be appropriate and interesting.<BR><BR>Our most recent poll has revealed that EQII players will probably choose their level 6 classes accordingly: Mage: 30%, Fighter 26%, Rogue 19%, Priest 15%, Tradesman 10%. Cast your vote now.<BR><BR>We have also compiled a complete list of the 16 races that will be featured in EverQuest II. New Race: Ratongas (rat men)<BR><BR>All this and more at - <a href="http://www.eqlounge.com/" target=_blank>http://www.eqlounge.com</A><BR><BR>Tomorrows's Updates: Comprehensive EQII Features List and Updated FAQ<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Ganza<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=384">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">EQ Lounge </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							There are (approx) 177 days left until EverQuest II is released.<BR><BR>According to a SOE executive, the beta will definitely begin this summer. If you would like to be notified when the EQII beta begins, simply visit the site and enter your email into the "Newsletter" box. <BR><BR>We would like to inform you that we just opened our EverQuest II discussion forums. The first thread discusses the likely hood and pros/cons of naming the EQII servers after the current EverQuest servers. Stop by and give us your thoughts. Feel free to start any new discussions you feel would be appropriate and interesting.<BR><BR>Our most recent poll has revealed that EQII players will probably choose their level 6 classes accordingly: Mage: 30%, Fighter 26%, Rogue 19%, Priest 15%, Tradesman 10%. Cast your vote now.<BR><BR>We have also compiled a complete list of the 16 races that will be featured in EverQuest II. New Race: Ratongas (rat men)<BR><BR>All this and more at - <a href="http://www.eqlounge.com/" target=_blank>http://www.eqlounge.com</A><BR><BR>Tomorrows's Updates: Comprehensive EQII Features List and Updated FAQ<BR>
							 <BR><BR>- Ganza<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=384">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, May 08, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Order of the Dragonborn </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Order of the Dragonborn is a Guild founded in November 2002 out of a bunch of friends who were not satisfied with their former Guild anymore. Now we are grown fast and took down several higher Mobs without big problems in particular (Cazic Thule, ToV-Nameds, PoP-Nameds..) We are focusing at the moment on hunting in Plane of Tactics, BoT, PoTorment, and also having the other old-world (Kunark,SoV,Luclin) mobs in mind.<BR><BR>We are still searching some members of several classes.<BR><BR>Level-Minimum is 56+ and the Classes are restricted to a maximum number of Characters (Check the Charta on the Homepage)<BR><BR>If you are familiar with your class (to know what are your do's and dont's) and if you like to see some higher mobs and still want a kind of family atmosphere (the friendship is a very big point in our guild!) check out the Homepage at http://dragonborn.serveftp.net
							<br><BR>
							 - Isharia<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=383">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Saturday, May 03, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Website up </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hail all, I am Trasque Twintone, a Co-leader of Noble Blood. I am just letting you know that we have a website up and running now. WWW.nobleblood.net, look us up!
							<br><BR>
							 - Trasque<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=382">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=382">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>

				</td>			
